2. **PLL Calculation**:
   - Source clock: HSI16 = 16 MHz.
   - Input division factor $M = 4$: bits `PLLM[3:0] = 3` (encoding $M - 1$). The resulting PLL input frequency is:
     $$f_{\text{PLL\_IN}} = \frac{16\text{ MHz}}{4} = 4.0\text{ MHz}$$
     This satisfies the input frequency specification $2.66\text{ MHz} \le f_{\text{PLL\_IN}} \le 16\text{ MHz}$ [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123].
   - Multiplier $N = 40$: bits `PLLN[6:0] = 40`. The resulting VCO frequency is:
     $$f_{\text{VCO}} = 4.0\text{ MHz} \times 40 = 160\text{ MHz}$$
     This satisfies the Range 1 VCO limits $96\text{ MHz} \le f_{\text{VCO}} \le 344\text{ MHz}$ [STM32G474_Datasheet p.123].
